<title>FRANCE: U.S. top destinations for Jan-Nov 96 Paris exports.</title>
<headline>U.S. top destinations for Jan-Nov 96 Paris exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States was the principal destination for export traffic from the Paris airports between January and November 1996 , Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The principal destinations by country for ADP exports during the period January-November 1996, with percentage change on January-November 1995, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  United States	  117,635 tonnes  up    0.7pct</p>
<p> 2  Japan		     30,047 tonnes  down  8.0</p>
<p> 3  Hong Kong		 22,734 tonnes  up    3.6</p>
<p> 4  Canada		    19,323 tonnes  down 20.4</p>
<p> 5  Germany		   18,688 tonnes  up   22.7</p>
<p> 6  UAE			 15,286 tonnes  up   28.8</p>
<p> 7  United Kingdom	  15,275 tonnes  down 15.8</p>
<p> 8  Brazil		    14,316 tonnes  down  3.4</p>
<p> 9  India		     13,730 tonnes  up    6.1</p>
<p> 10 Mexico		    11,153 tonnes  up   30.9</p>
<p> 11 French West Indies    10,822 tonnes  down  4.6</p>
<p> 12 Reunion		    9,350 tonnes  down  3.2</p>
<p> 13 Saudi Arabia	     9,305 tonnes  up    0.5</p>
<p> 14 Italy			8,678 tonnes  down  0.1</p>
<p> 15 Egypt			8,316 tonnes  up   11.4</p>
<p> 16 Singapore		  7,964 tonnes  up   15.8</p>
<p> 17 South Africa	     7,299 tonnes  up    4.8</p>
<p> 18 Korea			7,249 tonnes  down  2.2</p>
<p> 19 Thailand		   7,102 tonnes  down  9.0</p>
<p> 20 China			6,523 tonnes  down 15.5</p>
<p>    Total		    360,795 tonnes</p>
<p>Global January-November 1996 export traffic from the Paris airports totalled 537,878 tonnes down 0.9 percent on the same period the previous year, airport authority figures show. - Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
